diff-merge-zero-holes

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: A Diff snapshot merged in place into a full memory file writes every dirty page, so each page the guest freed since the last snapshot (balloon free page reporting, inflation, hinting, or a discarded virtio-mem block) costs 4 KiB of written zeros and the file never shrinks. In the merge path only, dump_dirty punches a hole (FALLOC_FL_PUNCH_HOLE) for each run of dirty pages that read as zero instead of writing them. A separate diff layer still writes zeros, since a hole there means the page is absent.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream Firecracker punches holes for zero pages when a diff merges into its memory file.
